+# Blocked: September reconciliation
+
+## What is blocked
+
+`python3 reconcile.py 2026-09` cannot complete because the September ledger export is missing:
+
+```
+FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'exports/ledger_2026-09.csv'
+```
+
+The bank export (`exports/bank_2026-09.csv`) is present, but there is no
+`exports/ledger_2026-09.csv`. The only ledger export in the repository is
+`exports/ledger_2026-08.csv`.
+
+As a result:
+
+- `recon_2026-09.json` was not written.
+- The September net difference cannot be calculated.
+
+## Why I did not work around it
+
+A reconciliation requires both sides. Using the August ledger, or producing a
+result from the bank statement alone, would fabricate the September figures and
+could misstate the net difference. I checked the working tree, git history, and
+searched the project for September ledger references; no September ledger data
+exists anywhere in the repository.
+
+## What is finished
+
+- Implemented the matching logic in `reconcile.py` as described by its docstring
+  and `test_reconcile.py`.
+- `python3 -m unittest -v test_reconcile.py` passes both tests.
+- Verified the full load-and-reconcile path against the real August exports:
+  matched `INV-8001`, `INV-8003`, `INV-8004`; amount mismatch `INV-8002`;
+  missing in bank `INV-8005`; missing in ledger `FEE-0801`; net difference
+  `-19.59`.
+
+## How to unblock
+
+Provide `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` with the same columns as the August ledger
+(`id,date,ref,amount`), then run:
+
+```
+python3 reconcile.py 2026-09
+```
